      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3524807571,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The later pipeline failed on macOS with\n\n```\n/Users/tuexen/builds/X_NM8olTA/0/wireshark/wireshark/wsutil/str_util.c:402:19: error: 'strchrnul' is only available on macOS 15.4 or newer [-Werror,-Wunguarded-availability-new]\n  402 |     return (char*)strchrnul(str, ch);\n      |                   ^~~~~~~~~\n/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/SDKs/MacOSX26.sdk/usr/include/_string.h:198:9: note: 'strchrnul' has been marked as being introduced in macOS 15.4 here, but the deployment target is macOS 13.0.0\n  198 |         strchrnul(const char *__s, int __c);\n      |         ^\n/Users/tuexen/builds/X_NM8olTA/0/wireshark/wireshark/wsutil/str_util.c:402:19: note: enclose 'strchrnul' in a __builtin_available check to silence this warning\n  402 |     return (char*)strchrnul(str, ch);\n      |                   ^~~~~~~~~          \n```\n\nThe reason why it's trying to use the system's `strchrnul()` is presumably that the \"is this available?\" checks are testing with a newer SDK that has it but the test somehow doesn't force it to say \"hey, we're building for Ventura and later, so, if it wasn't available in Ventura, it's not a thing\".",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
